{
  "_comment": [
    "Whatever shines, shining as hard as it can. `glow` is one name on the stars, the curtain and the bow, so",
    "this is the same word about all three and about anything that grows a glow later; on land, biomes and",
    "what grows it leans towards what is pale, well lit or gives off light of its own.",
    "",
    "It absorbed `glimmering`, which set the same glow (retired.json).",
    "",
    "`bright sky` is a pale, clear vault; a bright sun a larger one that glares a little, a bright moon a larger one with a halo; `bright underground` glows."
  ],
  "meanings": [
    {
      "sets": {
        "glow": "1.0..1.0"
      },
      "must_always_apply": true
    },
    {
      "leans": {
        "all": {
          "#bright": 0.8,
          "#glowing": 0.6
        }
      },
      "must_always_apply": true
    },
    {
